{"title":"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the sequence \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/f/f0fcd013ad1a54a0cb03908e97e712430fd7e69a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,-2,3,-4,5,-6,\\ldots,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"173\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>whose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/1/58116583f0a23d3e57ef83c277be9097a4989663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1)^{n+1}\\cdot n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"19\" />. What is the average of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> terms of the sequence?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9f2071724323ac117dd7bbe29f236e07145ec21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}-\\!1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}-\\!0.5\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 0\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 0.5\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"403\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The average of a list is the sum of all numbers divided by the size of the list.\n</p><p>The sum of the list can be found by adding the numbers in pairs:  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c96816276356b7a86394c6940e829487f4346e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 + -2) + (3 + -4) + ... + (199 + -200)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"322\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The sum of each pair is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> pairs, so the total sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060d8850e65d5781ce12d9fe2681f401dd6ee77c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> numbers on the list, so the average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/6/ca6ea84aa0ecf78e2f696b8d78d954b0f8b50678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-100}{200} = -0.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"106\" height=\"37\" />, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsect